  "nl_text": "This schema is for a simple e-commerce website. It consists of six tables: user, product, order, role, role_shipping_address, and order_details.\nThe user table contains information about the users of the website, including their username, password, contact information, and role. The role table contains information about the different roles that users can have on the website, such as administrator or customer.\nThe product table contains information about the products available on the website, including their name, description, price, inventory quantity, and image.\nThe order table contains information about the orders placed by users, including the order ID, user ID, total price, order status, order time, and shipping address ID. The shipping address ID references the user's shipping address in the role_shipping_address table.\nThe role_shipping_address table contains information about the shipping addresses of users, including the user ID, address ID, add time, and is default.\nThe order_details table contains information about the products included in each order, including the order ID, product ID, and quantity.\nAll tables have primary keys, and some tables have foreign keys that reference other tables. For example, the order table has a foreign key that references the user table, and the order_details table has foreign keys that reference the product and order tables. The foreign keys are set to cascade, which means that if a user or product is deleted, all related orders and order details will also be deleted.\nOverall, this schema provides a simple and organized structure for storing and retrieving data for a simple e-commerce website.",
  "gold_question": "The following is a description of the database requirements for the management system of an e-commerce platform:\n\nThe User module provides user registration, login, and personal information management functions. User information includes User ID, Username, Password, Contact Information, etc.\n\nThe Product module allows administrators to add, modify, delete, and categorize products. Product information includes Product ID, Name, Description, Price, Inventory, Images, etc.\n\nThe Order module handles order creation, viewing, modification, cancellation, shipping, and receiving. Order information includes Order ID, User ID, Product ID, Quantity, Total Price, Status, Time, etc.\n\nThe Shipping Information module manages user shipping addresses. Each user can have multiple shipping addresses and set a default shipping address. The Address Management module records detailed user address information. Address information includes Address ID, Province, City, Detailed Address, etc.\n\nThe Role Management module assigns different role permissions, such as administrator and regular user. Role information includes Role ID and Role Name, etc.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0143.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0143\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`role_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `role_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role_shipping_address` (\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `add_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `is_default` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`address_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `role_shipping_address_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `order_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `shipping_address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`shipping_address_id`) REFERENCES `role_shipping_address` (`address_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_details` (\n  `order_details_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_details_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_details_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_details_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
